  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cultural Transformation in Bogot&#xe1; for the Promotion of a Culture of Peace, Reconciliation and Non-repetition.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to address identified challenges related to the low technical capacities of collective reparation subjects and community organizations in protecting the rights of victims, weak coordination between local and national institutions, and limited community capacity for dialogue and memory construction. The project includes actions such as strengthening memory construction, training leaders, organizing cultural encounters, and developing a pedagogical strategy for peace. It also focuses on empowering children and adolescents in conflict-affected areas through workshops on peace culture and conflict resolution. By enhancing the capacities of collective reparation subjects, leaders, and youth, the project aims to promote collective memory, repair, reconciliation, and a culture of peace in communities. The goal is to ensure sustainability by enabling autonomous initiatives that contribute to territorial transformation, organizational strengthening, and local leadership.</narrative>
  </description>
